{
  "name": "Lacquer",
  "tagline": "Black lacquer, vermilion, gold leaf and abalone shell inlay",
  "story": "A lacquer box is built up coat by coat until its surface goes deep and still, then decorated with vermilion, sprinkled gold and slivers of abalone shell. Lacquer brings that box into the editor: a warm red-black ground, a cool shell-blue night, and a pale gold-leaf day. The grounds stay low-glare, and each syntax role gets its own pigment, so keywords, strings and numbers never melt into one another.",
